# Local development defaults, for `pnpm dev` and nothing else.
#
# `scripts/dev.mjs` loads this before turbo starts, so both the workspace and
# the worker get it. It does NOT override a variable that is already set, so
# reaching any other database stays a deliberate act: export it, or run it
# inline, and what you exported wins.
#
# That direction is the point. The root `.env` points at Supabase, which runs
# behind the migrations on a feature branch. If a bare `pnpm dev` picked that
# up, the README's local development section would quietly attach a dev server
# to the hosted database, and work on a new migration would run against a
# schema that does not have it.
#
# Committed, unlike every other .env, and nothing here is a secret. The
# passwords are the ones the migrations create and `pnpm db:setup` sets; they
# are already printed in `.env.example` and in the runbook; and they reach
# localhost:54322, which is the only place `db:setup` and `db:drift` will point.
# A gitignored file would mean a fresh clone has a dev server that does not
# start until somebody already knows why.

# The tenant query path. ranza_app is not an owner and has no BYPASSRLS, which
# is the whole point: policies are the authorization boundary, and a privileged
# connection switches every one of them off while appearing to work.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ranza_app:ranza_app@localhost:54322/ranza"

# Credentials, through a separate role (ADR 0005). ranza_app is granted nothing
# on the auth tables, so a defect in a tenant query cannot read a password hash
# or a session token.
AUTH_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ranza_auth:ranza_auth@localhost:54322/ranza"

# The outbox worker's own role (ADR 0018). It refuses to start if this equals
# DIRECT_URL, or if the role behind it owns a table, is a superuser or carries
# BYPASSRLS — so this cannot quietly become the migration connection.
WORKER_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://ranza_worker:ranza_worker@localhost:54322/ranza"

# Never a real secret, and it does not need to be: it signs sessions against a
# database that exists only on this machine. Same reasoning as the browser
# harness's own secret in playwright.config.ts.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="local-development-only-and-never-a-real-secret"
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
